= #text("Complete preserved v19 scientific record")

#text("The following complete record preserves the earlier scientific sections, negative results, equations, tables, algorithms, figures and appendices. Its development-stage statements retain their original scope. The current compact conclusions and detailed derivations precede this archived material; retaining an earlier result does not turn it into an independent replication.")

#text("SkillMerge: Agreement, Output Length and the Limits of Compositional Repair: From composition diagnostics to agreement, length controls and candidate-class selection")

#text("Neutral working paper v19, 2026-10-19. New finite saved-evidence diagnostics; no new independent data, real model/API calls, native-method trial or physical acquisition. Previous v17 evidence and v18 presentation are retained.")

#text("Can agreement between two useful skill outputs safely guide their composition? We distinguish this unexecuted behavioral question from an exposed SciFact-derived diagnostic bank. V17 retains 309 tasks, 204 components and 22,794 ordered pairs, executes five label-blind output constructors and controls their output lengths. Intersection-only raises exact-reference score against a longer left-union rule but loses sufficient coverage and is worse than a pairwise length-matched uniform subset on both endpoints. An explicitly post-primary controlled audit isolates common-item priority against the same round-robin baseline: zero sufficient gains and two losses, including a saved pair whose two inputs both contain valid alternative rationales. Five component folds always select round-robin for sufficient containment and intersection-only for exact matching, giving no score gain from changing the rule across folds. A gold-aware oracle is only an upper bound for the four predeclared selector candidates; an excluded negative control can exceed it and is not retrospectively promoted. Alternate author implementations verify 113,970 deterministic outputs and 25,119 exact uniform probability cells. All data are already exposed annotation-derived constructions. Independent A/B histories and qualified pairs remain zero and the behavioral composition effect remains null. The contribution is an auditable agreement/selection mechanism comparison with explicit information and cost boundaries. The continuation gives exact capacity-window identities and a conditional no-loss boundary, while first-three truncation and unit weighting retain important failures.")

- #text("A decision-focused formulation of qualified skill composition: joint availability versus the mean isolated branch, conditional on an independently applied qualification gate, with eligibility yield separated from effect.")
- #text("An executed evidence-contract audit preserving source connectivity, annotation alternatives, exposed-data status, and distinct task/component/response denominators.")
- #text("Budget-reachability and same-set controls that separate answer-space impossibility, annotation omission, ranking sensitivity, and actual semantic loss; exact finite controls are checked by exhaustive enumeration.")
- #text("A new executed complete-score-support analysis that turns endpoint disagreements into sharp fixed-cohort contrast-sensitivity envelopes, with separate qualification-cohort transport bounds and explicit worst-case versus behavioral-estimate distinctions.")
- #text("A falsifiable, equal-information and fully charged comparison protocol against conservative replay, typed migration, and assessment/assembly methods; agent effects remain unestimated rather than inferred from grader diagnostics.")
- #text("A constrained, fully replayed merge operator exposes a score-sign reversal on the same task cohort, separating monotone evidence union, ranked truncation and exact-set grading without inventing model histories.")
- #text("An exact order/capacity benchmark with annotation-blind controls, permutation-orbit bounds, a complete sufficient-failure partition and a symmetry counterexample to interpreting local reversal repairs as aggregate improvement.")
- #text("An executed label-blind agreement audit with pairwise length-matched random controls, component-disjoint rule selection, restricted-class oracle accounting and a post-primary controlled common-priority counterexample.")
- #text("A new predeclared finite audit keeps the round-robin relative order within common and noncommon IDs and only promotes the common class. For a nested output prefix L, the first sufficient capacity is the minimum, over complete reference alternatives, of the largest reference-ID rank. Two operators therefore differ in sufficiency on at most one contiguous capacity interval for a fixed pair. This is an annotation-containment identity, not a semantic claim about agreeing natural skills.")
= #text("Preserved v19: Introduction")

#text("Agent instructions increasingly live in reusable skill files with associated tools and resources. A deployment decision arises when two changes are useful separately: should both become available together, should integration be repaired, or should deployment fall back to an isolated branch? A negative score alone does not answer why integration failed. It could reflect lost evidence, different ordering under a ranked contract, an omitted valid annotation, changed tool rights, or additional context. Distinguishing these possibilities determines which intervention is worth deploying.")

#text("Consider an evidence task whose correct rationale contains three sentences. Two isolated configurations and their ancestor return these sentences followed by an irrelevant sentence; the joint configuration returns the same four IDs with the irrelevant one first. A first-three grader reports a strict joint failure, while full-set containment reports no change. If ranked evidence is the application contract, the failure is operationally meaningful. The identical full set nevertheless rules out the stronger explanation that the joint answer lost an annotated evidence sentence. A study that confuses these claims can prescribe the wrong repair.")

#text("Our question is therefore two-level. The behavioral target is whether independently qualified changes lose completion jointly. The completed empirical contribution is an audit of the measurement substrate required to investigate that target. This ordering follows established concerns about evidence evaluation ")#link(<bib1>)[#text("[1,3,4]")]#text(" and construct validity ")#link(<bib8>)[#text("[8,9]")]#text(", rather than claiming that measurement validity is newly discovered. The useful gap is operational: a claim about qualified composition needs a chain linking candidate history, held-out qualification, answer expressibility, grader behavior, and fresh deployment outcomes.")

#text("We ask three research questions. RQ1: do original valid annotation responses remain accepted, and is a complete answer expressible under the proposed budget? RQ2: which endpoint changes can occur while the full evidence set is fixed? RQ3: what additional histories, controls, and comparison rights are required before estimating a qualified-composition effect? RQ1 and RQ2 receive finite, executed answers; RQ3 receives an explicit prospective protocol. No observation in the completed audit qualifies a skill pair.")

#text("The v14 follow-up asks a sharper measurement question: given a task, a response budget and fixed arm outputs, how far could changing the endpoint move the composition contrast? Counting four particular order flips cannot answer that question, because those controls explore only selected responses. We therefore characterize all attainable simultaneous sufficient, first-three and exact scores within a declared response space. A sharp envelope over unrestricted response assignments can be calculated without inventing a single agent history. We also distinguish this same-cohort sensitivity from changing which candidate pairs qualify when the qualification grader changes.")

#text("Figure 1 separates these evidential stages. The completed lane contains 531 tasks, 309 evidence-bearing tasks, 548 annotation responses, and 4,186 constructed diagnostics. These are nested units, not independent integration events. The separate behavioral lane has zero authoring histories, zero eligible pairs, and a null effect. Our central practical result is that an incomplete grader and an unexamined response cap would already change eligibility and mechanism interpretations before any model comparison begins.")

#text("Figure 1 preserves the earlier measured-versus-prospective separation; Figure 4 adds the new response-space sensitivity analysis. The original 4,186 stored diagnostic rows are not relabeled as new model predictions, and the new abstract score cells are not qualifying events.")

#text("V15 asks which measurement patterns survive a concrete coupling between the isolated and merged responses. A union cannot independently choose an arbitrary response for each arm, and cannot invent a new sentence. By replaying that narrow operator we obtain a constructive control below the v14 worst-case envelope: a score decrease can arise from a nonmonotone endpoint even when evidence is preserved, while a capacity-limited union can actually drop the second input's evidence. Both statements can be tested before collecting real skill histories.")

#text("V16 then asks whether a visible ranking repair survives a symmetric cohort comparison. Exact prefix-subset enumeration separates reference availability, capacity and order, while annotation-blind controls expose an endpoint tradeoff. The key negative control is that reversing every ordered pair has zero aggregate gain even when it repairs every selected priority failure. Figure 6 links that finite result to the still unexecuted behavioral study.")

