== #text("Preserved v19: Response-space sensitivity is not observed disagreement incidence")

#text("Figure 4 reports the new support-envelope radii. At budgets one through three, sufficient and first-three give identical scores for every admissible response, so their fixed-cohort contrast difference is exactly zero. At budget four, 296 of 309 tasks support both zero and positive sufficient-minus-first-three discrepancy. Their equal-task radius is 296/309, approximately 0.957929, and it remains unchanged through budget ten. Equal-component weighting yields approximately 0.967320. The 13 remaining tasks have no such score variation in this response space. A large worst-case radius means annotation and endpoint structure alone cannot guarantee sign robustness; it does not mean models usually approach this extremum.")

#text("Sufficient versus exact has equal-task radii zero at budget one, 290/309 at two, 305/309 at three, 308/309 at four, and one from five onward. The unique four-sentence rationale is exact at four IDs and becomes a sufficient but nonexact response when an extra ID is permitted at five. First-three versus exact has radius 305/309 at budget three and one from four onward. All current taskwise radii are zero or one, although the adversarial family demonstrates that radius two is possible on a different annotation structure.")

#text("These results explain why the earlier four particular one-distractor order flips cannot be used as an overall error probability or sensitivity bound. Those controls expose four changes within their selected paired responses; complete response support allows other scored prefixes with no annotated rationale followed by a valid rationale. Conversely, zero sufficient/first-three sensitivity at budget three does not validate that budget: the earlier audit shows one original task whose four-sentence-only answer is unreachable for both graders. Agreement between endpoints can coexist with a common answer-space failure.")

#text("The envelope is calculated on the exposed development collection with declared weights. It is not R_Q for an unknown qualified population and cannot be substituted for theta_Q. A future same-output score rescoring can use its own arm-specific disagreements, which may cancel and be much smaller than the worst-case support radius. A future negative contrast is sign-robust only if its uncertainty and declared endpoint-sensitivity allowance support that conclusion. No such behavioral estimate or uncertainty interval exists in the current study.")

