#figure(figure-image("figures/merge-operator-contrast.svg", 248.756177pt, "skillmerge merge-operator-contrast"), kind: image, caption: [#text("New v15 deterministic response coupling. Ordered union has positive sufficient and negative exact-grading contrast on the same fixed task bank. Prefix3 exposes ranked capacity loss. All values condition on correct labels and constructed responses; no observed model interaction or independent sample claim.")]) <fig-merge-operator-contrast>

== #text("Preserved v19: Capacity and input order are distinct interventions")

#text("Prefix3 sufficiency exactly equals first-three union scoring on every pair, producing equal-task contrast +0.136890. Compared with untruncated sufficient union, capacity reduces that diagnostic contrast by 0.062854. This is an operator comparison over identical inputs, not a confidence interval or an inferred natural loss rate. The explicit full outputs distinguish actual sentence omission under truncation from mere endpoint rejection under exact grading.")

#text("There are 1,277 ordered pairs for which first-three union, equivalently sufficient prefix3, scores below at least one input. No pair loses when both inputs pass, because the A-prioritizing operator preserves all of A's at-most-three IDs. This asymmetry is built into the operator and explains why a both-pass criterion alone misses loss of an individually useful B when A fails. Both A,B and B,A are included so that this chosen prioritization remains visible.")

#text("One counterexample has A=[0,1,2], B=")#link(<bib3>)[#text("[3]")]#text(", with original rationale ")#link(<bib3>)[#text("[3]")]#text(". Ordered union preserves the rationale, its first-three score fails and a prefix3 output actually omits ID3. Reversing the inputs places ID3 first and avoids that particular capacity failure. In contrast, reordering a union containing two distinct exact alternatives cannot make its full set exact. A repair aimed at ranking and a repair aimed at the acceptance contract therefore address different causal constructions.")

#text("We independently recompute all 136,764 pair-by-endpoint/operator cells without importing the author scorer, checking all 1,854 task summaries and both-pass rejection counts. Idempotence, no invented IDs, distinct-ID caps, sufficient monotonicity and the exact/truncation counterexamples are executable assertions. These calculations validate the finite replay implementation on exposed annotations; they do not validate an authoring system or establish independent data.")

#text("The next behavioral experiment must keep the union and prefix controls as declared baselines, preserve every initiated authoring history, qualify A and B using Q without S feedback and evaluate all arms on S with explicit costs. Until those histories exist, actual_A_B_histories=0, eligible_pair_n=0 and the qualified interaction effect remains null. A response-bank replay cannot silently fill that denominator.")

= #text("Preserved v19: Exact order and capacity diagnostics")

#text("The v15 prefix counterexample leaves a tempting but incomplete prescription: reverse the two inputs. That repairs a chosen example, but what happens when every ordered pair is retained? We make this intervention explicit before claiming a better integration strategy. The research question now holds the available sentence set fixed and distinguishes a missing reference rationale, a rationale too large for the declared output, and a rationale that could fit but is excluded by one ordering.")

#text("The new plan and code are frozen with the exact earlier task measurements, diagnostic rows and v15 result before execution. We retain all 2,494 distinct at-most-three-ID input responses, all 309 evidence tasks, all 204 structural components and all 22,794 ordered pairs, including identical pairs. This continuation reuses exposed oracle-authored diagnostics. It makes 638,232 deterministic output replays across four controls and seven capacities; these are not new model predictions or independent behavioral trials.")

#text("Left union, right union, ascending document IDs and round-robin interleaving see only A and B. Each deduplicates the same union U and emits its first min(c,|U|) distinct IDs for capacities c=0 through6. Round robin interleaves A0,B0,A1,B1 and so on before deduplication; document order uses numeric sentence position rather than a relevance oracle. All controls therefore share the same available information and output-ID count for a given pair and capacity. Equal IDs do not imply equal tokens, inference cost, content quality or runtime.")

#text("For a uniform permutation of U, every size-k prefix subset is equally likely, where k=min(c,|U|). We enumerate these subsets rather than sample seeds. Sufficient and exact expectations use k; the first-three endpoint uses min(c,3,|U|). For every endpoint we also calculate the smallest and largest score over the orbit. Those extrema use annotations and belong only to the auditor. No policy receives the successful prefix or a gold-derived ordering.")

#text("The primary estimand is the equal-task mean score, averaging declared pairs within each task first. Equal-component and pair-pooled means remain separate sensitivities. We report score levels rather than silently changing the isolated-arm capacity in a new interaction contrast. The new code separately reproduces every one of the six v15 contrasts under its original alone-response contract. No endpoint is renamed as ERASER confidence-based sufficiency or an official SciFact leaderboard score ")#link(<bib1>)[#text("[1,2,4]")]#text(".")

$ k = min(c, |U|) $

$ P_("suff")(U,c) = frac("successful size-k subsets of U", "all size-k subsets of U") $

