= #text("Preserved v19: Agreement as a policy signal")

#text("V16 shows that a local input reversal can repair selected failures without improving the reversal-symmetric cohort. V17 asks a different operational question: can common evidence IDs supply a useful, label-blind composition signal? We keep the same 309 tasks, 204 recorded components, 2,494 inputs and 22,794 ordered pairs. Each constructor receives A and B only. Reference labels enter evaluation and training-component rule selection, never the output constructor. This remains an exposed diagnostic bank rather than independently authored skill behavior.")

#text("Let U be the distinct union, I its intersection and RR the deduplicated round-robin sequence. Agreement-first emits all common IDs, followed by RR noncommon IDs, then truncates to three. Agreement-only emits I without filling unused slots. Disagreement-first promotes the RR noncommon IDs before common ones and is declared a negative control. Left-union and RR retain their previous definitions. Fixed-count rules emit min(3,|U|) IDs; agreement-only emits |I|, possibly zero. Disagreement here means nonoverlap of IDs, not contradiction between scientific claims.")

#text("Agreement-only has a simple containment limitation. Because each A contains at most three distinct IDs, left-union truncated at three still contains all of A, while I is a subset of A. Any rationale contained in I is therefore also contained in left-union. Agreement-only cannot improve sufficient containment over left-union under this contract. Removing extra IDs can nevertheless improve exact-reference matching, so an exact-score increase need not indicate newly recovered information. Empty intersection is retained as a zero-score output, not omitted from coverage.")

#text("We compute two exact uniform-subset controls on the same U: length min(3,|U|), and length |I| for that particular pair. The second isolates whether the intersection selects unusually useful IDs after matching its shortened output count. These probabilities enumerate all equally likely subsets; they are not random model trials. ID-count matching does not equate tokens, inference access, bytes or elapsed cost. The conditional correct-label and supplied-document assumptions remain unchanged.")

$ I = A ∩ B $

$ I ⊆ A ⊆ L_(3) (A,B) $

$ S(I) <= S(L_(3) (A,B)) $

