== #text("Preserved v19: Threats to interpretation")

#text("Gold labels and rationale sets are privileged inputs. Their semantic correctness and completeness were not independently adjudicated. A sentence outside the annotation union is unannotated by construction; calling it irrelevant is operational shorthand, not a domain-expert judgment. Exact-annotated can reject valid unlisted evidence, and sufficient containment tolerates unhelpful extras. Our conclusions concern the specified annotation contract.")

#text("The study uses one exposed scientific-verification adaptation. Structural disjointness does not establish semantic independence or absence of model pretraining exposure. Four paired flips and one unreachable case are finite findings worth preserving, not a population prevalence claim. The related-work inspection is bounded to recorded primary passages; several references are preprints, one uses an abstract-only scope, and none supplies a reproduced external result. No external professor or independent scientific reviewer endorsed the results.")

#text("The elementary reachability proof and counterexample do not certify methodological novelty. We do not show a new integration controller, general harm from skills, or superiority over the cited systems. The falsifiable contribution is narrower: concrete admissibility checks and controls prevent unsupported inferences in the planned qualified-composition experiment. Full reference scopes, local provenance, and reproducibility limits are preserved in the appendices and companion records.")

#text("The new support certificate is complete only under the declared ordered-ID response contract and its checked outside-union condition. It does not adjudicate unannotated valid rationales or model-generated labels. Its sharpness permits arm/task-specific response choices, without common-program, routing, qualification or learning constraints. These deliberately weak behavioral restrictions make the envelope conservative for actual skills and unsuitable as an empirical rate. Changing benchmark annotations, response validity, weighting or Q selection requires a new certificate or transport analysis. The total-variation bound additionally requires common preselection weights and fixed candidates; it does not absorb authoring changes or final-data feedback.")

= #text("Preserved v19: Conclusion")

#text("Before asking whether useful skills fail together, specify which outcomes would count and whether valid answers can be expressed. On the preserved SciFact adaptation, original alternatives, a three-ID cap, and evidence ordering change diagnostic acceptance in quantitatively different ways. These results support grader-admission decisions and narrower mechanism claims. Qualified composition remains a separate empirical question: with zero actual histories, its effect is null. The next defensible advance is an independently qualified, freshly evaluated behavioral study with strong conservative comparisons and complete accounting.")

#text("The new v14 analysis closes a narrower gap: it computes exact response-support envelopes and distinguishes their fixed-cohort meaning from qualification-cohort transport. The observed zero envelope at budgets at most three and the large budget-four worst case change how a future score sign should be audited. They do not supply missing qualified histories. The next decisive evidence remains an independently authored, fully charged A/B-to-S experiment with an unchanged declared task contract.")

#text("The constrained v15 replay adds a concrete falsification control: a sufficient-score gain and an exact-score loss coexist under a sentence-preserving union, while a three-ID cap introduces real omission. This is a measurement-and-operator result. It narrows what a future negative behavioral score would mean without supplying the still absent qualified histories.")

#text("The v16 orbit benchmark makes one repair claim precise: reversing priority fixes all selected cap-three losses but cannot improve a reversal-symmetric cohort. Matched simple controls and an exhaustive reference-conditional failure partition locate a future intervention's burden of proof. Round-robin containment gains with exact-match losses remain finite development evidence; qualified behavioral effects still await independent histories.")

#text("V17 shows that common-ID agreement, shortening and model selection require separate controls. A same-RR priority intervention has two actual sufficient failures; intersection-only trades coverage for exact agreement and still trails a length-matched random subset. Component cross-fitting adds no score over its stable fixed choices. The oracle is restricted to four predeclared rules, while excluded negative-control results remain diagnostic. None of these finite findings identifies a qualified behavioral skill-composition effect.")

#text("V19 identifies the capacity mechanism more precisely. Completing an alternative reference set is controlled by its maximum output rank; a stable common-item promotion creates at most one contiguous gain or loss window. For two individually annotation-sufficient inputs of length at most three, full-sufficiency loss is impossible at cap four or above. First-three scoring can nevertheless retain the earlier losses, and cap-one pooled and equal-component contrasts have opposite signs. These exact conditional statements refine the finite mechanism claim; they do not establish a behavioral effect of independently authored executable skills.")


