= #text("Completeness and sharpness of the new response-support certificate")

#text("Let the annotation family be nonempty and contain no empty set; let d be an ID outside its union. For any response L, T(L) and E(L) imply U(L). The empty response witnesses (0,0,0) at cost zero. If E(L)=1, its full set equals an annotation R. Enumerating each min(3,|R|)-ID prefix subset of R enumerates every possible T score for that exact set, so the recorded minimum length is complete for (1,0,1) and (1,1,1).")

#text("If U=T=1 and E=0, the scored prefix contains an annotation R of size at most three. Any such nonexact response has length at least |R|+1. The response R followed by d has exactly that length, keeps U=T=1, and cannot equal any original annotation because d occurs in none. This proves both attainability and minimum length for (1,1,0).")

#text("If U=1,T=0,E=0, L has at least four IDs. Its three-ID prefix P contains no annotation, and some annotation R lies in L. Let W=P union R. If W is not an annotation, P followed by R minus P is a witness no longer than L. If W is an annotation, L must have at least one further ID because L is not exact. Appending d to the reduced witness therefore still fits within |L|. The prefix remains unsuccessful and the outside ID guarantees nonexactness. Exhausting P and R is consequently complete and retains a minimum-length (1,0,0) witness. These five cases exhaust all possible patterns. The outside-union assumption is necessary for this particular reduction argument; its failure must be detected rather than hidden.")

#text("For discrepancy e_t(L)=g(L)-h(L), the change in a three-arm mean-isolated contrast is e_t(L_AB) minus half the sum of e_t(L_A) and e_t(L_B). This lies in the interval from m_t-M_t to M_t-m_t. Finite support attains both endpoints by choosing minimizing/maximizing witnesses. Because no cross-task or cross-arm realizability restriction is imposed, nonnegative fixed weights preserve sharpness after summation. Imposing a shared learned program or information constraints can shrink the attainable set, so the certificate remains an outer bound rather than a claim that qualified agents attain it.")

#text("For two selected distributions derived from the same original weights, their common probability mass after normalization is r/max(q_g,q_h). Total variation equals one minus that overlap. A bounded function in [-1,1] has expectation difference at most twice total variation, attained by assigning +1 and -1 according to the sign of the distribution difference. An authored three-history example checks equality. If an admission mass is zero, normalization is undefined and no point effect or overlap correction is supplied.")

= #text("New execution and a bounded candidate-history pilot contract")

#text("The canonical new result is runs/research_advancement_v14_20261019_01/skillmerge/bounds_01/results.json, SHA-256 f70e47a5b1455cfe27a85f8dcb6ac31e11a205221519aa5f99a030173b74d106. The adjacent receipt binds the locked plan, code and input snapshots. The validation_01 sibling preserves a separate verifier snapshot, input lock, result and receipt. The published source manifest records exact paths and byte hashes; these are reproducibility bindings, not proof of annotation truth or external replication.")

#text("A proposed next feasibility pilot uses three independently sourced task families and four independent authoring attempts per family: twelve attempted A/B histories, not a power-calculated confirmatory sample. The two authors receive the common ancestor, public D information and identical tool rights, but not each other's patch or auditor-only Q/S labels. Cap each branch at two proposals and preserve every rejection, invalid proposal and failed call. Before authoring, freeze the actual model identity, request/token/cost limits, rationale contract and tokenizer-aware budget. Use twenty source-disjoint Q tasks per family and one predeclared seed; require each isolated branch to exceed the same ancestor by at least two successful tasks out of twenty. Freeze all capped proposals before Q and return no Q feedback to their authors. An auditor chooses the first passing proposal in the predeclared proposal order for each branch, not the best final-S result. With one ancestor and at most four branch proposals, qualification costs at most one hundred task-arm executions per history, before charged generation and tool work. This is a fixed feasibility rule, not a powered significance test, and permits no final-S repair. The number of eligible pairs is an outcome: do not relax the gate if it is zero.")

#text("For each eligible pair, a bounded first S phase would assign four fresh reset arms on twenty unexposed tasks per family with two predeclared seeds per arm, up to 160 final task-arm-seed executions per pair. Twenty tasks and two seeds are feasibility caps, not an asserted precision or independence guarantee. A third party or user must provide genuinely unexposed source histories/tasks, and the evaluation package must preserve their access log. Record all four frozen outputs before endpoint rescoring, a union-of-Q-gates cohort ledger if testing qualification changes, complete availability/routing/read/assembly traces, rejected proposals and total resource use. This protocol is unexecuted and requires separately authorized model/data-transmission limits; the current offline run initiates none of those calls.")

